   "tests": [
    {
     "id": "convect_deep_step18",
     "description": "The physics_update law at the convect_deep call site (proc zm_conv_tend, physpkg.F90 tphysbc), step 18, pinned from the cam_phys_tend.csv / cam_phys_tend_q.csv rows (step 18, site convect_deep, all 9 dumped constituents) at the ZM-active levels only (dump lev 15..32; steps 1-17, 24-39 and 41-48 carry all-zero ptends at this site and are not pinned, and levels 1-14 are pinned nowhere because the law leaves them unchanged). Exercises: the T update T + ls*ptend_s*dt/cpairv, the u/v updates, the constituent update with the qneg3 floor (qmin table of chemistry.F90) and the number-concentration clamp min(max(q,1e-12),1e10) for NUMICE/NUMLIQ/NUMRAI/NUMSNO (fires at NUMICE across the column), the state_cnst_min_nz(1e-36) zeroing of the (CLDLIQ, NUMLIQ) and (CLDICE, NUMICE) pairs (fires at CLDLIQ on ~29 of 32 levels), and the geopotential recompute asserted via zm_after/s_after.  cld_min_nz = 1 at CLDLIQ/CLDICE because the site's proc name zm_conv_tend is in cldlim_names (physics_types.F90:246-247). Expected values chained to the next call site's dump rows (step 18, site convect_shallow: state_before(convect_shallow) == state_after(convect_deep), verified for the whole 48-step window by stage1/analysis/extract_cam_physics_update_pins.py).",
