   "tests": [
    {
     "id": "tend_accumulation_bc_step18",
     "description": "The tend accumulation of the whole tphysbc phase, step 18, pinned as a multi-site sum over the 15 consecutive tphysbc physics_update calls (energy_fixer, dadadj, convect_deep, convect_shallow, ssatcontrail, clubb#1..3, microp#1..3, aero_calcsize, aero_wetdep, convect_deep_2, radiation; the CLUBB/MG2 rows already carry the 1/3 macmic pre-scaling, so summing the dumped rows reproduces the accumulation) against the cam_tend_total.csv phase=bc row: dtdt = accumulated ptend_s/cpairv, dudt/dvdt = accumulated ptend_u/ptend_v (physics_types.F90:289-300, 417-419). The input is the per-site tendency of every call; the expected value is the independent phase-total dump column, so the assertion fails if the window gating, the flag gating or the summation is wrong. The accumulation is linear in the calls, so the sum over the 15 sites is bit-identical to the bc row (worst rel err 0, verified by stage1/analysis/extract_cam_physics_update_pins.py). The ac-phase dtdt is NOT pinned: after the last physics_update call the SE dycore rescales tend%dtdt by cpairv/cp_or_cv_dycore (physpkg.F90:2026-2030), a documented gap (README-cam-physics-update.md).",
